# PRESERVE-AND-CAP inside an EXPLODED CONTAINER (canon call 2-bis).
#
# A list that carries an interior comment falls back to one element per line
# with a trailing comma. `format_bracketed_broken_with_comments` had no blank
# emitter, so every author paragraph break BETWEEN elements was deleted — 341 of
# `compiler/data/resources.gg`'s 353 blank lines are this one cell.
#
# AXIS: where the blank sits relative to the leading-comment run × run length ×
# position in the list.
#   (a) blank between two COMMENT-FREE elements     → kept        [was DROPPED]
#   (b) blank ABOVE a leading comment               → kept, ABOVE [was DROPPED]
#   (c) blank BELOW a comment                       → kept, in place (unchanged)
#   (d) blank BETWEEN two comments                  → kept, in place (unchanged)
#   (e) a nested exploded list                      → the same rule recursively
# The two cells that are NOT fixed points — a 2-run capped to one, and a blank
# right after the OPEN delimiter, which is dropped because the rule is keyed on
# the PREVIOUS element rather than on an index — live in the sibling fixture
# `exploded_containers_collapse.gg`, asserted against an exact expected text.
#
# ⚠ (b) IS THE CELL THAT ACTUALLY OCCURS. At this commit the emitter is only
# reachable through the interior-comment gate, and `resources.gg` — the file
# this change exists for — has a leading comment above EVERY element with the
# blank above it. So the comment-free cells are the ones reality does not
# contain, and (b) is the one that pays.
#
# ⚠ (b) ALSO PINS AN EMISSION ORDER, not just a count. `blank_line()` runs
# BEFORE `emit_comments_before`, the order every clause and member emitter
# keeps. The inverted order yields the IDENTICAL blank COUNT, so only a
# positional assertion can tell them apart — measured: with the two swapped,
# each comment detaches from the element it documents and glues to the element
# above it. This fixture is a FIXED POINT, so it sees that.
#
# RED against the pre-change binary, measured: cells (a) and (b) came back with
# the blank deleted; (c) and (d) were already correct and pin no-regression.
void main():
    Vector[int] xs = [
        # first group
        1,
        2,

        3,

        # second group
        4,
        # a comment with a blank below it

        5,
        # first

        # second
        6,
    ]
    Vector[Vector[int]] nested = [
        # outer head
        [
            # inner head
            7,

            8,
        ],

        [
            # inner tail
            9,

            10,
        ],
    ]
    print(xs.len() + nested.len())
